## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design live vocabulary updates without downtime and without compromising inference determinism or latency.

## Key Concepts
- Online feature/versioning strategy
- Atomic swaps and read/write separation
- Embedding vocab management for high-cardinality features
- Rollback, monitoring, and drift testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: atomic vocab switch in a minimal preprocessing shim
class VocabCache {
  constructor(a,b) { this.current = 'A'; this.maps = { A: a, B: b }; }
  lookup(cat){ const map = this.maps[this.current]; return map[cat] ?? map['<UNK>']; }
  swapVersion(next) { this.current = next; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift and decide when to promote vocab?
- How would you test hot-swap under burst traffic and ensure P95 latency stays within target?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of production-grade model serving, stateful components, and zero-downtime updates under streaming data.

## Key Concepts

- Embedding sharding and stateful serving
- Online updates without stale reads
- Atomic model version swaps and canary deployment
- Observability, SLAs, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: versioned embedding cache lookup
const version = process.env.MODEL_VERSION || 'v1';
const embedCache = loadEmbeddingCache(version);

function predict(inputIds) {
  const emb = embedCache.lookup(inputIds);
  return model.apply(emb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test zero-downtime swap guarantees?
- What race conditions could arise and how would you mitigate them?
